  "unit": "Offensive possession, linked to the five players on the court for the offensive team at the start of the possession.",
  "sample": "All offensive possessions from NBA 2022-23, 2023-24, and 2024-25 regular seasons and playoffs. Focus on possessions immediately following a substitution that changes the offensive five, or comparing possessions of distinct lineups of the same team.",
  "power": "A priori power analysis will be conducted to determine the minimum detectable effect size for shot mix changes (e.g., 1 percentage point shift in 3-point attempt rate) given the available data. If the sample size for specific lineup changes is too small to detect meaningful effects, the scope will be limited to more frequently used lineups or aggregated player archetypes.",
  "controls": "Mixed-effects model (e.g., linear regression for proportions or multinomial logistic regression for categories) with: 1. Team fixed effects to control for overall team offensive philosophy/talent. 2. Opponent fixed effects to control for defensive scheme/talent. 3. Game fixed effects to control for specific game contexts. 4. Score margin and time remaining as continuous covariates. 5. Lagged shot mix (from previous possession) to control for autocorrelation. 6. Player fixed effects (or individual player on/off adjustments) within lineups to disentangle individual player tendencies from lineup-specific emergent effects. 7. Lineup fixed effects where sufficient data exists for specific five-man units. 8. Defensive matchup information (e.g., presence of a rim protector on the floor).",
  "falsification": "1. Placebo test: Analyze the effect of *random* (non-personnel-changing) event boundaries on shot mix to ensure no spurious correlation. 2. Reverse causation check: Test if future shot mix predicts past lineup changes. 3. Sensitivity analysis: Vary definitions of 'shot mix' (e.g., different zone boundaries) and control variables to check robustness of effects.",
  "multiplicity": "Adjust p-values for multiple comparisons if testing effects across many shot mix categories or lineup changes (e.g., Bonferroni correction or FDR control). Prioritize a primary outcome measure (e.g., 3-point attempt rate or rim attempt rate) to minimize multiplicity issues.",
  "decision_rule": "The hypothesis is supported if there is a statistically significant (p < 0.05 after multiplicity adjustment) and substantively meaningful (e.g., >1 percentage point shift) change in shot mix attributable to offensive personnel changes, consistently observed across robust analyses and falsification checks.",
  "data_version": "NBA 2022-23, 2023-24, 2024-25 regular season and playoffs. Per-game files from NBA stats API: play-by-play, substitution rotation intervals, starters, defensive matchup minutes and partial possessions, box-score summary. Derived play-type possession records from a graph database."
 }

